    understand the two procedures: MO_RF(TRF).gver (left): proc gver(x : text, t : text) : bool = { var test : text; var 
     b : bool; if (x \in seen) { b <- false; } else { test <@ TRF.f(x); b <- test = t; } return b; } MO_O.gver (right): 
proc gver(x : text, t : text) : bool = { var test, v : text; var b : bool; if (x \in TRF.mp) { b <- false; } else { v
<$ dtext; TRF.mp.[x] <- v; b <- v = t; } return b; } Key differences: 1. Guard: x \in seen (left) vs x \in TRF.mp 
(right). Under the pre MO_RF.seen{1} = fdom TRF.mp{1}, these are equivalent (by mem_fdom). 2. Then branch: same (b <-
false). 3. Else branch: - Left: calls TRF.f(x) which (for TRF) checks if x in mp, if not samples from dtext and sets
     mp[x] - Right: samples v from dtext, sets TRF.mp[x] = v The result on left: b <- (oget TRF.mp[x]) = t The result on 
  right: b <- v = t where v = oget TRF.mp[x] after setting Since…

