 The call (_: ={res, TRF.mp}) fails because res is not a recognized variable in the invariant. In pRHL, res refers to 
the procedure's return value, but in a call invariant, you need to use the return variable name or res in the post. 
Actually, for call (_: P), P is the invariant for the procedure call. After the call, the post is P /\ ={res}. So the
call invariant should just be ={TRF.mp} (since gver returns a value and call automatically adds ={res}). Let me fix:
call (_: ={TRF.mp}) instead of call (_: ={res, TRF.mp}):

